  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/post/src/post/explain.rs`: `explain()` reads a post's own word meanings before the mill table. Manifest `explainWords` maps a G / M word to a text (`\"\"` = leave unexplained) or `{ said, takes }` - a word explained only beside the value word it folds in (Fanuc lathe `G50 S4000` -> `SPINDLE SPEED LIMIT 4000`; `G50 X Z`, the coordinate setting, says nothing). `explainTool = \"station-offset\"` reads T0101 as `TOOL 1, OFFSET 1` (T0100: `NO OFFSET`; any other T form is silent, never guessed). A malformed table is refused by name before any hook, only when Explain is on (`Script::explain_refusal` in `js.rs`).\n- `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`: states G98 = feed per minute, G99 = feed per revolution, G50 with S, and the T reading. `tormach-lathe.cps`: the T reading (it writes G95, not G98/G99). Manifest globals only - neither post declares `explains` yet (#1387 / #1388 wire that), so no posted program changes.\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`: the two globals documented. Decision: `docs/decisions/1399-lathe-explain-words.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `crates/post/tests/explain_lathe.rs` (fails on the old code: TOOL 101, CYCLE RETURNS, no refusal):\n  - `fanuc_lathe_explains_its_own_feed_modes_tool_word_and_speed_limit` - the shipped fanuc-lathe.cps with a test shim (`explains = \"paren\"`, `block()` appending `explain()`), a CSS turning section and a C-axis live section: T0101 / T0202, G50 S, G98, G99 read the lathe way; no mill reading anywhere; Explain off is byte-identical to the shipped post; every Explain-on line is its plain line plus one comment.\n  - `a_lathe_word_without_its_reading_is_left_unexplained_never_guessed` - G50 without S, T0100, T1, tormach-lathe T0303, and a mill post keeping G99 = R-height / T101 = tool 101.\n  - `a_malformed_word_table_is_refused_by_name_only_when_explain_is_on`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green (post suites 23 s incl. explain, script_fanuc_lathe, script_tormach_lathe; app lathe/post suites 231 s). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No shipped post explains yet, so no real lathe program carries the comments; the wiring (#1387 / #1388) will hit the 60-character cap on fanuc-lathe's opening block (G99's meaning falls past it, by the existing whole-meaning cut).\n- Release-tier heavy lanes, ui suites; Windows only.\n\nChangelog: Explain G-code reads a lathe post's own words: G98/G99 as feed modes, T0101 as tool 1 offset 1, G50 S as the spindle speed limit (#1399)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1399\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
